@namespace PgmStudio.Client.Components

@* Everything the pointer can do to the map, floating at the bottom centre where the pointer already is.

   The dock holds groups, never loose buttons: a group is one question the tool answers (how do I get around ·
   what do I draw · what do I measure with), and the gaps between them are the only grouping a row of equal
   glyphs can carry. Groups wrap upward on a narrow viewport rather than scrolling sideways, so the last group
   is never the one that disappears.

   While a group's flyout is open the dock lays a scrim over the canvas, so the click that dismisses the
   flyout is the same click anywhere else — and it lands on the scrim rather than starting a drag on the map
   the author could not see past the menu. *@

@if (FlyoutOpen)
{
  <div class="canvas-dock-scrim" @onclick="OnDismissFlyout"></div>
}
<div class="canvas-dock">@ChildContent</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Whether one of the dock's collapsed groups is showing its flyout.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool FlyoutOpen { get; set; }
    /// <summary>Fired when a click lands outside the open flyout.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnDismissFlyout { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
